  "reason": "Evidence: RNA is clearly the dominant signal (RNA-only multiprofile avgpool: 0.591 vs image-only singleprofile: 0.208), and the best config so far (config_019, multimodal/multiprofile/pca_n2000/resnet50/avgpool/weighted at 0.639) relies entirely on PCA as the RNA encoder. The RNA encoder is the single largest unexplored design axis, and since RNA drives most of the performance, improving it has the highest potential payoff. Question tested: Does a learned single-cell latent representation (scVI, 200-dim) outperform a linear PCA (2000-dim) in the multimodal setting? config_031 is a minimal, controlled change from the best config—only the RNA encoder is swapped—so any performance shift is cleanly attributable to the encoder choice. Why best next: It directly extends the strongest evidence we have, tests the highest-leverage unexplored variable, and its outcome (whether learned representations help or PCA suffices) will guide all subsequent multimodal experiments, making it the most information-dense use of the next budget slot."
}

